          "id": "india-e20-karnataka-claims-2026-11-07",
          "headline": "Petroleum Ministry says E20 petrol meets standards, rejects Karnataka's claims",
          "summary": "The Petroleum Ministry and state-run IOC, BPCL and HPCL say all 893 E20 petrol samples tested in 27 states and UTs meet the BIS standard, including 56 from Karnataka with 19-20% ethanol. Karnataka had said some pumps sold petrol with 26-31% ethanol; the oil firms say its tests skipped legal sampling rules and have asked for joint testing.",
          "why_it_matters": "The row between the Centre and a big state over fuel quality feeds doubts about India's ethanol-blending push.",
          "importance": 3,
          "lead": false,
          "verified": false,
          "note": "Claim by the Petroleum Ministry and state oil companies; Karnataka's own test results have not been independently checked.",
